# Draft-commit git-log style (persistent)

This file was written by `/crav1-draft-commit-message` when you chose **existing git log style, this commit and onward**.

When drafting or creating commits in this repo:

- Match **this repository’s** recent `git log` (subjects and bodies), not CRAV1 style (`crav1-draft-commit-message/references/style.md`).
- Do not switch to Conventional Commits unless the live log already uses that shape.
- Do not ask whether to use git-log style. It stays on until this rule is removed.

**To stop and get the style prompt again:** delete this file. Claude Code project: `.claude/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.md`. Claude Code user: `~/.claude/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.md`. Nothing else to undo.

